CRC32-CRC32-CRC32-CRC32-CRC32-CRC32-CRC32-CRC32-CRC32-CRC32-CRC32-CRC32

Primarily: if you don't know what is CRC32 then you don't need it :)
As I couldn't find CRC32 in 68k assembler I have decided to release
that one. It's little bit optimised compiler output, alas CRC32 due
to heavy memory usage should fly only on faster boards...

